course: dictionary
lesson: 15519
title: Subsistence: just enough to live on
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Subsistence means having just enough food, water and money to stay alive, with nothing extra. Look at the clues in this sentence: «The family grew beans and rice only for themselves, with nothing left over to sell.» Nothing is left over, so subsistence means just enough.
explain: The word is also used for farming. Subsistence farming means growing food to feed your own family, not to sell. Commercial farming is the opposite: farmers grow crops and animals to sell for money.
explain: In money talk, subsistence can mean the money paid to cover basic costs. «The company paid her a subsistence allowance for her meals and hotel on the work trip.» The money is only for the basics, like food and a bed.
fact: Subsistence means having just enough food, water and money to stay alive, with nothing extra.
fact: «Subsistence farming» means growing just enough food to feed your own family, not to sell.
fact: «A subsistence level» means living with only the basics, like food and water.
fact: «Means of subsistence» means the way a person gets the things they need to stay alive, such as farming or a job.
fact: «Subsistence allowance» is money paid to cover basic costs like meals and a hotel when you are away for work.
exercise: «The village farmers grew only enough maize to feed their own families.» What does subsistence farming mean here? | Keeping animals as pets | *Growing just enough food to feed your own family | Building new homes for the village | Growing food to sell in shops around the world
exercise: Sam's aunt went to a city for work. «Her company paid a subsistence allowance for meals and a hotel.» What does a subsistence allowance pay for? | New cars for the team | Tickets to the football match | *Basic living costs like meals and a bed | Presents for her family
exercise: Which word means having just enough food and water to stay alive, with nothing extra? | Surplus | Luxury | Profit | *Subsistence
test: «In the old village, many families lived at subsistence level.» What does subsistence level mean? | Living in a big house by the sea | *Having just enough to stay alive, with nothing extra | Having a lot of money saved in the bank | Having more money than they could spend
test: Which one describes commercial farming? | Fishing in a lake for a picnic | Growing food only for your own family | Keeping bees for fun in the garden | *Growing crops and animals to sell for money
exam: «Pedro grows only enough food for his family, so his farm is a ___ farm.» Choose the word for the gap. | *Subsistence | Busy | Commercial | Desert
